# Projects and favicons

## Where the repos live (local machine)

All site repos are siblings under:

`C:\Users\18057\Documents\Projects\`

They appear together in the Cursor sidebar when that folder (or a multi-root workspace) is open. Do **not** search GitHub or the web to find them — look in the sidebar / that path.

## Favicon source kit (this repo)

Complete favicon bundles live in `favicons/<site>/`:

| Folder | Site | Status |
|--------|------|--------|
| `favicons/badboards/` | badboards.org | Done |
| `favicons/keristokstad/` | keristokstad.com | Done |
| `favicons/toolkit-badboards/` | toolkit.badboards.org | Pending |
| `favicons/civiccongruence/` | civiccongruence.org | Pending |
| `favicons/decathecting/` | decathecting.com | Pending |
| `favicons/honor-flight/` | honor-flight / keristokstadwrites.com | Pending |
| `favicons/communitymediavoices/` | communitymediavoices.org | Optional (already set) |
| `favicons/orrerymap/` | orrerymap.com | Optional (already set) |

Each bundle contains: `favicon.svg`, `favicon.ico`, `favicon-16x16.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png`.

Build scripts: `scripts/build-favicons.sh` (one site), `scripts/build-all-favicons.sh` (all sites).

## How to add a favicon to any site

1. Open the target repo from `Documents/Projects/` in the sidebar.
2. Copy all 4 files from the matching `favicons/<site>/` folder into that repo's `public/` (Vite/Next) or site root (static HTML).
3. Add to `<head>` after `<title>`:

```html
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
```

4. Remove any default Vite/Next/Vercel favicon. Commit and push.

## Important

- Do **not** ask the user to run scripts unless they want to rebuild from PNG masters.
- Do **not** use vague prompts like "do keristokstad.com" — open the specific repo folder and edit only `public/` (or root) + `index.html` / layout metadata.
- Private repos may not appear on GitHub search; use the local sidebar path above.
